🔹 Program 16: Employee Payroll Mini-Project

📌 Description

This program demonstrates run-time polymorphism in an employee payroll system.

"Employee" is an abstract base class containing the pure virtual function "calculateSalary()".

Two derived classes are created:

- 👨‍💼 "PermanentEmployee"
- 👨‍💻 "ContractEmployee"

Each class calculates salary differently.

The "printPaySlip()" function accepts an "Employee" reference and calls the appropriate "calculateSalary()" implementation at run time.

🎯 Concepts Used

- 🔹 Abstract class
- 🔹 Pure virtual function
- 🔹 Inheritance
- 🔹 Run-time polymorphism
- 🔹 Function overriding
- 🔹 Base-class reference
- 🔹 Virtual destructor

💡 Key Point

Different employee types can be processed through the same "Employee" interface while providing their own salary calculation.
